<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick I, Elector Palatine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1425–<a href="/years/1476">1476</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Frederick the Victorious</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick I, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elector-palatine">Elector Palatine</a>, called the Victorious, governed the Palatinate from 1451 as guardian of his nephew and then as elector in his own right. He defeated a coalition of neighbouring princes at Seckenheim in 1462. His morganatic marriage to Clara Tott produced the counts of Löwenstein, ancestors of the Löwenstein-Wertheim line.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-i-elector-palatine.jpg" alt="Frederick I, Elector Palatine" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Albrecht Altdorfer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Friedrich_der_Siegreiche_von_Albrecht_Altdorfer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
